1. flat model: Laplacian of G away from the pole = 0 ; flux through a sphere = 1
2. J(t) = int_{G=t} |grad G|^3 = 32*pi**(3/2) * t^(5/2);  32 sqrt(w5) = 32*pi**(3/2) ; equal: True
   so int_0 J(t) t^(-sigma-1) dt converges exactly for sigma < 5/2 (integrand t^(3/2 - sigma))
3. flat model volume of {G > t}: V(t) t^(3/2) = 1/(48*pi**(3/2)) ; 1/(48 sqrt(w5)) = 1/(48*pi**(3/2)) ; equal: True
4. |B^6| = w5/6: True
5. (V^(-2/3))' bound: (2/3)*36*(w5/6)^(1/3) equals 24 (w5/6)^(1/3): True
6. (13.4): [24 (w5/6)^(1/3)]^(3/2) equals 48 sqrt(w5): True
7. threshold for J_inf: 32*pi**(3/2) ; equals J_pole = 32 sqrt(w5): True
8. flat model: J(t) * (-V'(t)) = 1  (Cauchy-Schwarz is an equality)
   flat model: -V' / |d{G>t}|^2 = 1 ; |dO| / (6 (w5/6)^(1/6) |O|^(5/6)) = 1
